@page "/"
<PageTitle>OpenConnect Developer Portal</PageTitle>
<HeadContent><meta name="description" content="Build secure .NET AI applications with OpenConnect and Microsoft Agent Framework." /><meta property="og:title" content="OpenConnect Developer Portal" /></HeadContent>
<section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">.NET-first · privacy-first · MAF-native</p>
    <h1>Build AI applications, not AI infrastructure.</h1>
    <p>OpenConnect gives ASP.NET Core applications secure composition, privacy enforcement, durable application boundaries and reusable client components around Microsoft Agent Framework.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/docs">Read the documentation</a><a class="button" href="/tutorials/todo">Run the Todo sample</a></div>
</section>
<section class="cards" aria-label="Portal capabilities">
    <article><h2>Static by default</h2><p>Documentation remains available without a database, worker, model provider or interactive circuit.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Native MAF</h2><p>OpenConnect composes Direct, Harness and Workflow capabilities. It does not replace the Agent Framework runtime.</p></article>
    <article><h2>Secure integration</h2><p>Privacy, tenant scope and tool authorization stay at the trusted .NET host boundary.</p></article>
</section>
